[size=5][b]InfinitePatch[/b][/size]
Modern PC fixes for BioShock Infinite, set in one [b].ini[/b] file. No game file is modified.

[b]Fixes[/b]
[list]
[*]Borderless fullscreen at your native resolution: no alt-tab lag, low latency and VRR on Windows 11
[*]No more crash after the intro videos on PCs with an integrated GPU (Ryzen 7000/9000, Intel)
[*]No framerate drops with 1000 to 8000 Hz mice, same mouse sensitivity when sprinting
[*]UI scaling for 1440p and 4K, FOV slider up to 105°
[*]Intro videos skipped, VSync or FPS cap, optional graphics tweaks (shadows, depth of field, motion blur)
[/list]

[b]Install[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Launch the game once, then close it.
[*]Extract the zip into the game folder (the one with [i]Binaries[/i] and [i]XGame[/i]).
[*]Run [i]Install.bat[/i]. Run it again after editing [i]InfinitePatch.ini[/i] or after a Steam update.
[/list]
[i]Uninstall.bat[/i] restores your original settings.

Source code and full documentation: [url=https://github.com/literalynn/InfinitePatch]github.com/literalynn/InfinitePatch[/url]
